@endnode

@node Menus "Using the menus"
@{b}Using the menus@{ub}

The File menu contains:

  * About MintSCAN... shows the installed program version and project details.
  * Quit closes MintSCAN.

The Help menu contains MintSCAN Help..., which opens this guide in
MultiView or an installed AmigaGuide viewer.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Requirements "Requirements"
@{b}Requirements@{ub}

  * Motorola 68000 or later.
  * AmigaOS 3.0 or later.
  * A running TCP/IP stack providing bsdsocket.library.
  * An eSCL/AirScan scanner reachable over plain HTTP.
  * About 1 MiB of free memory is recommended.

MintSCAN requests a 128 KiB stack. Use the supplied MintScan.info when
starting from Workbench. Scanned image data is streamed directly to the
destination file rather than being held completely in memory.

HTTPS-only _uscans devices are not supported in 1.1.0 because AmiSSL has
not yet been connected to the eSCL client.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Installation "Installation"
@{b}Installation@{ub}

Double-click Install and select a destination drawer, or copy the MintSCAN
drawer manually wherever you prefer. The installer copies only MintSCAN,
its icon, this guide and the licence. It does not install a driver or
change any AmigaOS system files. No reboot is required.

Saved profiles are written to ENV:MintSCAN/Unit0 through Unit7 and to the
matching ENVARC: files for persistence after reboot.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node QuickStart "Quick start"
@{b}Quick start@{ub}

  1. Start your TCP/IP stack.
  2. Run MintScan.
  3. Click Discover, or enter the scanner IPv4 address and click Query.
  4. Confirm that Model and Status are populated.
  5. Choose Source, Colour, DPI, Format and Size.
  6. Choose a destination with Browse or type an AmigaDOS path.
  7. Click Scan.
  8. Use Save Config if you want to retain the settings in this Unit.

The Scan button is disabled while the operation is running. A successful
scan ends with the exact byte count and destination in the message box.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Profiles "Scanner profiles"
@{b}Scanner profiles: Unit0 to Unit7@{ub}

Each Unit is an independent saved scanner profile. A profile stores:

  * IPv4 address, port and eSCL resource root.
  * Scanner model.
  * Source, colour mode, resolution, format and page size.
  * Destination file path.

Select a Unit, configure or discover the scanner, and press Save Config.
Switching to another Unit loads its saved values immediately. There is no
separate Activate step because MintSCAN has no background driver.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Options "Scan options"
@{b}Scan options@{ub}

Source
  Flatbed (Platen) or Feeder (ADF). Version 1.1.0 retrieves one page only;
  it does not loop through a multi-page feeder job.

Colour
  Colour (RGB24), Grayscale8 or BlackAndWhite1. MintSCAN validates colour
  modes against the selected source when the scanner advertises them.
  Brother MFC-J6930DW firmware advertises BlackAndWhite1 but returns a
  damaged RGB image, so that model alone is changed to Grayscale8.

DPI
  100, 150, 200, 300, 400 or 600. If the chosen value is not advertised
  for the selected source, MintSCAN uses the closest supported value and
  reports the substitution.

Format
  JPEG, PNG or PDF. The scanner creates the file; MintSCAN does not decode
  or convert it.

Size
  A4, Letter, Legal or A3. These are fixed request sizes. They are not yet
  derived from the scanner's maximum bed dimensions.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Saving "Saving files"
@{b}Saving files@{ub}

Type an AmigaDOS path such as RAM:scan001.jpg or use Browse to open the
standard ASL save requester. Changing Format updates the filename extension.

Existing files at the chosen path can be replaced. MintSCAN now checks every
disk write and the HTTP transfer framing. Disk-full, write, timeout and
truncated-transfer failures remove the partial destination instead of
reporting it as a successful scan.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Discovery "Discovery and manual Query"
@{b}Discovery@{ub}

Discover sends an mDNS query for _uscan._tcp.local. MintSCAN reads the
advertised DNS-SD SRV port and TXT rs= resource path instead of assuming
port 80 and /eSCL for every scanner.

Some emulators and routed/VLAN networks do not pass mDNS multicast. Enter
an IPv4 address, optionally followed by :port, and click Query in that case.
Manual Query uses the conventional /eSCL resource root.

HTTPS-only _uscans._tcp services are intentionally not displayed because
1.1.0 cannot connect to them yet.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Status "Status and error messages"
@{b}Status and error messages@{ub}

After a successful Query, the Status field shows the top-level eSCL scanner
state where supported: Idle, Processing, Testing, Stopped or Down.

The message box reports discovery, selected substitutions, job creation,
download progress and errors. If ScanJobs fails, MintSCAN queries
ScannerStatus again so an HTTP error can include the scanner's own state.

All connect, send and receive operations are timeout-bounded. A sleeping
Wi-Fi scanner receives one additional connection attempt.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Limitations "Known limitations"
@{b}Known limitations in 1.1.0@{ub}

  * Plain HTTP eSCL only; no HTTPS/AmiSSL yet.
  * One page per scan; no multi-page ADF loop or duplex.
  * Source, format and page-size choices are fixed lists.
  * Capability XML is deliberately parsed lightly rather than with a full
    XML library.
  * Manual Query accepts IPv4 and optional port, not hostnames or IPv6.
  * There is no cancel button during an active scan.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Troubleshooting "Troubleshooting"
@{b}Troubleshooting@{ub}

Nothing appears after Discover
  Enter the scanner's IPv4 address and click Query. This is expected with
  WinUAE SLIRP and networks which do not pass multicast.

Query times out
  Confirm that the scanner supports eSCL over HTTP and that its web service
  is reachable from the Amiga VLAN. Wake the scanner and retry.

Wrong DPI or colour
  Read the Requesting line in MintSCAN's message box. It shows the value
  actually sent after capability validation.

File will not open
  Check that the selected format matches the filename extension. MintSCAN
  1.1.0 rejects incomplete transfers, but scanner firmware can still return
  a valid container containing bad image data.

For difficult scanner firmware, run windows_escl_probe.py from the source
repository on a PC connected to the same network.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node Reporting "Reporting a problem"
@{b}Reporting a problem@{ub}

Open an issue at:

https://github.com/boingball/MintSCAN/issues

Include the scanner make/model, AmigaOS version, TCP/IP stack, source,
colour, DPI, format and size. If possible also attach the output from:

python windows_escl_probe.py SCANNER-IP --dpi 400 --color Grayscale8

Do not include credentials or unrelated network configuration.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode

@node History "Version history"
@{b}1.1.0 - 02 September 2026@{ub}

  * Eight saved scanner profiles.
  * Timeout-bounded connect, receive and send with Wi-Fi wake retry.
  * Live ScannerStatus display and clearer job errors.
  * ASL Browse requester and improved GadTools layout.
  * DNS-SD SRV port and TXT rs= endpoint discovery.
  * Complete-transfer and disk-write validation.
  * Model-scoped Brother BlackAndWhite1 workaround.
  * Added 400 DPI, installer, AmigaGuide and guarded release packaging.

@{b}1.0.0@{ub}

Initial working eSCL scan-to-file implementation.

@{"Back to contents" LINK Main}
@endnode
